    "body": "> So it's not just that we'd want to add a check as the first substep of navigate step 20, but we'd also check in between literally every in-parallel step...\r\n\r\nIndeed, actually, since I reported this issue, I already had to add a check to see if navigable is destroyed in some other places in my implementation.\r\n\r\n> I guess the predicate to check would be, is navigable's active browsing context non-null. Right? Because navigable itself is still around, captured by the spec's \"closure\". And there's no actual \"destroyed\" predicate on navigables.\r\n\r\nYes, that sounds right.\r\n",
